    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a39127da_25520e2a",
        "filename": "board/servo_micro/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 359,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291807
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-02T22:07:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "command_enable_ite_dfu() does not set all of them.  Which it sets could change as needed.  IMO it\u0027s cleanest for that function to only change the specific bits it wants to modify, and keep the full reset separate here.\n\nAFAIK nothing else uses these timers on Servo Micro today.  But not resetting all their registers prior to use would be a bug waiting to happen, should these timers get used elsewhere.  Best to be defensive.",
      "parentUuid": "441499d9_6e4a907b",
      "revId": "bf3d7d392472c74198367681671c0330c5985697",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
